  "description": "meme-id: nationalism_is_beauty_feminism_isnt; hasOverallIntent: Propaganda; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a crowd of diverse, joyful fans waving national flags and celebrating, visually representing unity and pride associated with nationalism. The overlaid text contrasts this with the assertion that 'feminism isn't,' implying feminism is inferior or less desirable. This juxtaposition is used to propagate a specific ideological message: that nationalism is inherently positive and beautiful, while feminism is not. The meme leverages the positive emotional association of national pride to implicitly discredit or diminish the value of feminism, suggesting it lacks the same aesthetic or moral appeal. This is a form of propaganda designed to influence viewers' opinions by equating nationalistic fervor with beauty and contrasting it with feminism, potentially reinforcing negative stereotypes or biases against feminist movements. The visual of diverse, happy fans is used to frame nationalism as universally appealing and wholesome, while feminism is implicitly portrayed as lacking this quality, which can be seen as a form of ideological manipulation.",
